  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (0.5203) outperforms pca_n2000 (0.4849) by ~3.5% in single-profile RNA-only setting, and image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.2079), suggesting RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: we have not yet tested scgpt, a more expressive RNA encoder, and it is unclear whether it can push accuracy beyond scvi_n200. This experiment (config_007: rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) isolates the encoder effect while holding profile setting and modality constant, directly comparable to config_004. Establishing the best single-modality RNA baseline before exploring multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion is critical: if scgpt substantially improves, subsequent multimodal experiments should use it; if not, scvi_n200 remains the anchor. With 6 experiments left, locking in the best RNA representation now maximizes the value of later fusion and aggregation experiments."
}

